privateData.editorialMd:
Build pairSums

`readings` is already sorted from smallest to largest. Pair its first and last numbers, then its second and second-last numbers. Keep moving toward the middle. Add the two numbers in each pair and record that sum. If one middle number is left, record it by itself. Keep this pair order in `pairSums`.

Return the answer

Find the largest number in `pairSums`. Store it in `largest`. Complete `facingCardsPeakTicket` so it returns `largest`. Return it, do not print it.

Why this works

Each value in `pairSums` follows task 1. The later tasks use only those values. Keeping these steps separate helps avoid returning the list when the question asks for one number. Check empty input, one item, repeated values, and the largest allowed input.

Efficiency goal: time O(n); extra memory, including the helper list, O(n). n is the input length. These labels describe how work and memory grow with the input.

